{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And these are the garments, etc.</b> It is difficult: why does the verse enumerate only six garments and omit the tzitz of holiness and the michnesayim? Perhaps the verse alluded to both of them: the tzitz it alluded to in the verse preceding this one, <b>And they shall make the garments of Aharon to sanctify him</b> — for there was no need to say anything other than ״ואלה הבגדים״ etc., but it intended the tzitz which it did not mention in the verse ״ואלה הבגדים״. Therefore it said ״לאהרן״ and did not mention his sons, because it intended only the tzitz. And it said it in plural language, because it alone is of no avail, for the eight garments are mutually interdependent; therefore it spoke of it in plural language. And from this it may also be deduced that it said <b>ואלה</b>, which appears to be adding to other garments — since it had already commanded concerning some of them, and there was no need to explain, for it relied on what it would later detail one by one; and when detailed you will find the allusion explained. And corresponding to the michnesayim: after it mentioned ״אלה הבגדים״ etc., it said <b>And they shall make garments of holiness for Aharon your brother and for his sons</b>, and this verse is superfluous — to speak of the michnesayim; and therefore it mentioned <b>Aharon and his sons</b>, because the michnesayim are required both for the Kohen Gadol and for the ordinary kohen." "Now it remains to know why the verse did not arrange them together with the six, and would not have needed all this. Perhaps these two things are not in one category with the six: the tzitz, on account of its superiority over the three garments of the Kohen Gadol, and therefore it was set apart on its own beforehand; and the michnesayim, on account of their being on a lower level than the three garments of an ordinary kohen, and therefore it was delayed to its own section afterwards; and the six are on an equal level." "Further, it appears that there is another reason for His doing so: that He intended to say that the priestly garments must be made לשמן (for their name/designation). Therefore it specified in the verse <b>And they shall make garments of holiness</b> — which we explained as referring to the michnesayim — and it said <b>for Aharon your brother and for his sons, to minister to Me</b>, meaning that they must be made for the name of Aharon, to minister before HaShem; and from this you learn [the same requirement] for the rest of the garments. And in the first verse, which we explained as referring to the tzitz, it said <b>to sanctify him</b> etc. — for besides the requirement to make it for the name of priesthood, it further adds and writes on it ״קדש לה״״."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:05.287099038Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}